# Wave T49 (Bridgeport kit): harbourbell — the ferry bell: a brass bell on an iron harbour post with its rope, rung for the crossings, seated at (16,12) on the pier's land side beside the shipped crates (15,12) — the harbour sign's own beat made dressing: 'The ferry captain keeps the long crossings at the pier.' Fully opaque: the town grass is baked in (measured #0d8420, tg-canalave's rendered pure flat). (NO-SAME-KIT law; WAVE-T49-BRIDGEPORT-PLAN.md §5.)
